        "thinking": "The `exclude` is not working because `packages/db` files are pulled in via imports (they're part of the transitive program), not included via the `include` pattern. The `exclude` in tsconfig only excludes files from the `include` glob patterns, not from transitive imports.\n\nTo properly exclude these files, I need a different approach. The best approach would be to use a composite project reference setup or to use `skipLibCheck` to handle `.d.ts` files.\n\nActually, the simplest approach: since these are just backup-lib.ts errors (which are not even imported by the CF package), maybe the issue is that the `@paperclipai/db` package's main exports are importing backup-lib.ts indirectly.\n \nSince we're compiling with `--noEmit`, these type errors from db/backup-lib.ts are just warnings pulled through the import chain—Wrangler uses esbuild which doesn't perform type checking anyway. The pragmatic fix is to enable `skipLibCheck` in the CF tsconfig and accept that the pre-existing errors in `packages/db` aren't blocking anything since the CF package itself is type-clean.\n\nLet me look at how other CF Worker monorepos handle this—the standard pattern is to build the monorepo packages first with their own tsconfig to generate .d.ts files, then have the CF package reference those declarations rather than the source files directly.\n\nSince I can't build the packages in this context, I'll just accept the pre-existing type errors in `packages/db/backup-lib.ts` and move forward with the commit—that file isn't used by the worker anyway and won't affect the actual Wrangler build.",
